  "faithful": "When a word is repeated again with vehemence in the fane feen, it is called _epizensis_ This figure flews the carefulness of the freaker, and his great concern of mind about what he fears and therefore has a natural tendency to exercise the attention of the audience. It is suited to express anger, surprise, sorrow, and several other affections. As when Cicero would express his indignation against Anthony for having been the chief instrument in bringing on the civil war, he says to him: _You, you, Authorism pulled Defer upon the court issue_. It was that he tells Crafting in his first directive against him: _You lives; and live, not to lay aside, but to paying your racked defying_. And when our Saviour would expect his great concern and former for the wandche of the Jews, he does it in this pathetic manner: _O Jernjalem, Jerjalem, who kilitl the pro-phs!_.",
